# Open files via the chat chip

Do **not** give markdown links (`[label](path)`) for the user to open a file or canvas. Those do not create the Open control above the chat. On Windows they also break (`\r` in `C:\Users\rft30\...`).

This overrides the Cursor canvas skill’s “always markdown-link the `.canvas.tsx`” instruction in this workspace.

## Do this instead

When the user needs to open a file or canvas, **touch it with an editor tool** in that turn (Write, StrReplace, or a small Read) so Cursor shows the file/canvas button above the chat.

- Canvas: Write/StrReplace on the `.canvas.tsx`. That is what creates the canvas Open button.
- After an external script patches a canvas (Python, not this editor), do a **header-only** StrReplace so the chip appears.
- `deco-helper-block-list.canvas.tsx` is ~2MB of icons. Do **not** Read the whole file. Header-only StrReplace is enough.

## Do not

- “Click this link to open…”
- File-tree instructions as the only way to open a canvas we just changed
- Dumping a Windows `C:\...` path in a markdown link
